  "question": {
    "text": "A point moves in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi></math> plane according to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>–</mo><mtext>cos</mtext><mi>ω</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>ω</mi></math> are positive constants. The distance traversed by the point during the time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>τ</mi></math>&nbsp;is"
  },
